      "replies": [
        {
          "id": "UgxXSIWe-6wJE1uDXx94AaABAg.AcMDhGnAifwAcQGqQf9P9v",
          "author": "@Globallife.documentary",
          "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/UT4yqZ2DrZ2fBIIQWOCcVrQYBje265v4HWuZn65ElT3j5IRtHyIw-Ezzb6kX6kLSxPFTaiT5EkE=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
          "text": "Warmest greetings all the way to Tuktoyaktuk, Northwest Territories! Kazakhstan's journey—from surviving brutal nuclear tests and devastating famines to rising from the wreckage and building futuristic marvels like Astana—truly shows how deep human resilience can run. What was your biggest takeaway from our deep dive into Kazakhstan?",
          "likeCount": 0,
          "publishedAt": "2026-10-26T07:38:55Z"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "UgxP-qGZfHO0myKogLl4AaABAg",
      "author": "@BestGlobalTravelDocumentary",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/sXMrYMCSGWX-pZEdDhzuG_gkQ7uq3dg0OHH4SpZvHZ-lEX8J1V9sA6HISwE03tUtjTeHx52QxQ=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "This documentary completely changed the way I see Kazakhstan. From the ancient nomadic traditions and incredible eagle hunters to the futuristic skyline of Astana, this country is full of surprises. The beauty of Kaindy Lake and those vast deserts is absolutely breathtaking. But what impressed me most was Kazakhstan’s decision to give up the world’s fourth-largest nuclear arsenal and choose peace. Such a powerful story of courage, resilience, and hope. Kazakhstan deserves so much more recognition! 🇰🇿❤",
      "likeCount": 4,
      "publishedAt": "2026-10-24T15:35:36Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
    },
